# [DD-13b.W1.1 r46sem finding 16] `flags i` BEFORE ANY `pattern` LINE, in
# a HEADLESS file. Legs A and B already refuse it ("'flags' line before
# any pattern block"); leg C used to fall through to its ordinary `flags`
# branch, get appended to `results`, and be silently DROPPED by
# `dump_file`'s `if blk is None: continue` -- accepting a directive with
# no block to attach to.
flags i
pattern a+
m "aaa" 0 3
